# Files consumed by Linux tooling must keep LF endings regardless of the
# checkout platform. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would hand a
# CRLF copy to scp, and the failures are opaque: a CRLF shebang aborts with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and a CRLF env file gives every
# value a trailing carriage return (PDF_INSPECTOR_BIND=0.0.0.0:8080\r).
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.env       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
